      "writtenOn": "2020-11-17T20:20:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "what does \"current installation\" mean when there are multiple stacks. it seems to me that \"voltha down\" should still remove everything. if we want to only tear down a stack then maybe \"voltha down \u003cstack-name\u003e\". This is sort of why I was going down the path of having multiple commands.\n\nvoltha env \u003cname\u003e up/down # or infra\nvoltha stack \u003cname\u003e up/down # for specific stack operations\n\nI worry that overloading the simply `voltha` command will confuse people.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1114,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1114,
        "endChar": 97
      },
      "revId": "689cf0a1af98a48c033e9f068b4ec6a8ca9d4a77",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
