    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0e5e0a03_3477c6d0",
        "filename": "voltha",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 1114,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000007
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-11-23T19:55:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "what I mean is that if you do:\n- VOLTHA_NS\u003dvoltha1 ./voltha up\n- VOLTHA_NS\u003dvoltha2 ./voltha up\n- VOLTHA_NS\u003dvoltha1 ./voltha down\n\ncomponents in both namespaces are removed. We should only remove components in the namespaces we specify.\n\nIt\u0027s also true that this will never really tear down a single \"stack\" with the current implementation and we keep talking to move to a more helm-centric approach, thus I changed the FIXME to a NOTE and we\u0027ll decide how to address this once we decide the direction kind-voltha will move toward",
      "parentUuid": "5b7cf9d6_de7a6fb6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1114,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1114,
        "endChar": 97
      },
      "revId": "689cf0a1af98a48c033e9f068b4ec6a8ca9d4a77",
