      "writtenOn": "2020-11-23T19:55:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is something we can debate on, without that when you remove a cluster the ports remain reserved, with that we free them for reuse.\n\nI added that as if I do:\n- NAME\u003dminimal ./voltha up\n- NAME\u003dminimal ./voltha down\n- NAME\u003dinfra ./voltha up\n\nThen all the port-forwarding have different values (eg: ONOS will on 8281) and I find that annoying (I have a bunch of commands stored that contains the port). I would be interested in knowing what other people point of view on this is.",
      "parentUuid": "411cf992_1071b8f0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1119,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1119,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "689cf0a1af98a48c033e9f068b4ec6a8ca9d4a77",
