    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b56a1cf_ff0bb4fe",
        "filename": "voltha",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 1119,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000003
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-11-25T00:31:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So ports are reused if I do\nvoltha up\nvoltha up\n\nbut not if i do\nvoltha up\nvoltha down\nvoltha up\n\nif we are not going to reuse ports in some cases is it better never to reuse ports and remove the code above that attempts to reuse them? \n\nmy concern is that by using the .ports file in this way, i think, it is possible to have things become inconsistent where if we either never or always reuse there is less chance.",
      "parentUuid": "7aab429b_d97bef35",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1119,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1119,
        "endChar": 71
      },
